  "details": "This *could* just be a desktop thing and it's definitely just a small issue, but; VelocityX and VelocityZ seem to be capped at 4.17/-4.17, and it's been that way for awhile, like years now.\n\nIdk if it's a bug, or if it's supposed to be that way -because VelocityY works perfectly-, but it's a problem for more in-depth locomotion animations.\n\nSay you move faster than the usual 4 m/s straight forward and you think jogging at 15 m/s looks weird, so you want to make a fast sprint animation instead of the usual jog, you have to sit a 10+ m/s sprint at 4.17 VelocityX in the blendtree or it will never trigger bc the parameter for some reason never goes above that, and if you only move slightly above 4.17 m/s instead of something like 8-10 m/s, you get the reverse moonwalk issue, where the animation of any reasonable sprint is to be moving faster than the actual movement, like walking on ice.\n\nDefinitely a small peev, but I would appreciate a change to it, if it's not capped for any particular reason.",
